---
description: Publish every site change to the live Worker and to staging
alwaysApply: true
---

# Deploy to Cloudflare Workers

Until the user says to stop, every completed site or UI change is published to both Workers. Deploying only the live site is not done.

They are separate Workers. A live deploy does not update staging.

1. Live Worker `hiweb-marketing-ui` (https://hiweb.com.mx). Unset staging env vars first, or this build is published to the wrong Worker:

```
Remove-Item Env:PUBLIC_SITE_ENV, Env:CLOUDFLARE_ENV, Env:PUBLIC_SITE_URL -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
$env:PUBLIC_SITE_URL='https://hiweb.com.mx'
npx astro build; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
npx wrangler deploy --keep-vars
```

2. Staging Worker `hiweb-marketing-ui-staging` (https://staging.hiweb.com.mx). Run this only after the live deploy finishes. `CLOUDFLARE_ENV=staging` has to be set during the Astro build. The adapter writes `dist/server/wrangler.json` for that environment. Without it, `wrangler deploy --env staging` publishes the bundle to the live Worker.

```
Remove-Item Env:PUBLIC_SITE_ENV, Env:CLOUDFLARE_ENV, Env:PUBLIC_SITE_URL -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
$env:PUBLIC_SITE_ENV='staging'; $env:PUBLIC_SITE_URL='https://staging.hiweb.com.mx'; $env:CLOUDFLARE_ENV='staging'
npx astro build; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
npx wrangler deploy --env staging --keep-vars
Remove-Item Env:PUBLIC_SITE_ENV, Env:CLOUDFLARE_ENV, Env:PUBLIC_SITE_URL -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
```

- Always pass `--keep-vars` so existing Worker secrets stay in place.
- Do not run the live build, the staging build, and `npx sanity deploy` at the same time. All three write `dist/`.
- Do not deploy Studio unless the change is a Sanity schema or Studio UI the editors need.
- Do not commit or push unless the user asks.
- Keep `PUBLIC_SITE_INDEXABLE` false.
- After both deploys, confirm https://hiweb.com.mx and https://staging.hiweb.com.mx. Staging returns 401 until the staging password is sent.
- If the browser still shows the previous version, tell the user to reload with Ctrl+F5.
